 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Previously, Arkady playfully wrestled with Lyosha in the communal apartment and ended up hurting his back. Meanwhile, at Ivan Samsonov's flat, Ivan tries to make peace with Nina by offering her an extra concert ticket.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Нина, у меня есть второй билет.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Завтра вечером в городе концерт.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nina",
   "t": "И что ты предлагаешь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Если ты хочешь, пойдём вместе.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nina",
   "t": "Вот это настоящий мужчина!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nina",
   "t": "Какой ты деликатный и добрый!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Значит, ты согласна пойти?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nina",
   "t": "Нет, конечно! Я не пойду.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nina",
   "t": "Лучше сходи с Клавдией Викторовной.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Она же меня совсем не любит.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nina",
   "t": "А я люблю тебя ещё меньше!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Спасибо за честный ответ, Нина.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's see how Nina responds to Ivan's awkward peace offering.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Нина, у меня есть второй билет.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Nina, I have a second ticket.' Ivan awkwardly attempts to make peace with an offering.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Завтра вечером в городе концерт.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Tomorrow evening there is a concert in town.' The adverbial phrase sets the time and venue.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nina",
   "t": "И что ты предлагаешь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And what are you suggesting?' Nina asks skeptically about his real intentions.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Если ты хочешь, пойдём вместе.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'If you want, let's go together.' The conditional clause expresses an informal invitation.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nina",
   "t": "Вот это настоящий мужчина!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Now that is a real man!' Nina responds with heavy dripping sarcasm.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nina",
   "t": "Какой ты деликатный и добрый!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'How tactful and kind you are!' The exclamatory adjectives mock Ivan's sudden politeness.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Значит, ты согласна пойти?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Does that mean you agree to go?' Ivan gullibly misreads her sarcastic remarks as genuine.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nina",
   "t": "Нет, конечно! Я не пойду.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'No, of course not! I won't go.' Nina quickly dashes his hopes with a blunt refusal.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nina",
   "t": "Лучше сходи с Клавдией Викторовной.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Better go with Klavdia Viktorovna.' Nina sarcastically suggests the elderly neighbor instead.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Она же меня совсем не любит.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'She does not like me at all, after all.' Ivan points out the bad blood between them.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nina",
   "t": "А я люблю тебя ещё меньше!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And I love you even less!' Nina emphasizes her bitter exasperation with him.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Спасибо за честный ответ, Нина.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
